---
// CopyMarkdown.astro — Copy Markdown button for doc pages, floats to the right
---

<button id="copy-markdown-btn" class="copy-markdown-btn" type="button">
  <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
    <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"/>
    <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/>
  </svg>
  Copy Markdown
</button>


<style>
  .copy-markdown-btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
    background: var(--sl-color-bg-inline-code);
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    float: right;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 1.5rem;
    transition: background 0.2s ease, color 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  }
  .copy-markdown-btn:hover {
    background: var(--sl-color-accent);
    color: #ffffff;
    border-color: var(--sl-color-accent);
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.25);
  }
  .copy-markdown-btn.copied {
    background: var(--nu-orange);
    color: #ffffff;
    border-color: var(--nu-orange);
  }
</style>

<script>
  const MARKDOWN = `# Nulang Language Reference for AI Agents

Nulang is a distributed, actor-based programming language written in Rust (repo: dporkka/nulang, Apache 2.0). It fuses Erlang-style fault-tolerant actors with a Hindley-Milner type system, row-polymorphic algebraic effects, and Pony-inspired reference capabilities.

## Architecture
- Compiler pipeline: Lexer → Parser → TypeChecker (Algorithm W) → EffectChecker → CapabilityAnalyzer → HIR → MIR → bytecode
- Two backends: Bytecode VM (default), Native AOT (--backend native), WASM (--backend wasm|wasm-run|wasm-aot)
- Register-based VM: 32-bit fixed-width instructions, 256 registers per frame
- JIT: Cranelift-based tiered compilation, hot-counter threshold 1000
- Runtime: single-threaded cooperative scheduler, crossbeam deques, ORCA GC with cycle detection

## Type System
- Hindley-Milner inference with row polymorphism for records and effects
- Reference capabilities: iso, trn, ref, val, box, tag, lineariso (compile-time only)
- Effect rows: every function carries an effect row (!{IO, State})
- Algebraic effects: perform, handle, resume — compose without monad transformers

## Actor Model
- Erlang-style: spawn, send (!), receive, link, monitor, trap_exit
- Supervision trees: one_for_one, one_for_all, rest_for_one, simple_one_for_one
- Location transparency: ActorAddress = Local | Remote(node_id, actor_id)
- Gossip-based cluster membership, 8 CRDT types with delta-state replication
- Per-actor GC (64KB bump-allocated heaps), no global stop-the-world

## AI Runtime (src/ai/)
- agent declarations with model, system_prompt, tools, memory config
- Provider-agnostic: OpenAI + Ollama
- Three memory subsystems: episodic (turn window), semantic (vector embeddings), procedural (learned patterns)
- Multi-agent: Pipeline (sequential stages), Debate (pro/con + moderator), Supervisor teams (OTP-style restart)
- Non-blocking LLM calls in actor behaviors via suspend/resume

## CLI
\`\`\`bash
cargo run -- --repl                    # REPL
cargo run -- --eval '<expr>'           # Evaluate
cargo run -- --check file.nula         # Type-check only
cargo run -- file.nula                 # Compile + run
cargo run -- --backend native file.nula # AOT compile + run
cargo run -- --backend wasm file.nula  # WASM compile
cargo run -- --lsp                     # Language server
\`\`\`

## Key Files
- src/vm.rs — Value (i64-tagged u64), Frame, VM, callback traits
- src/runtime/mod.rs — Runtime god-object
- src/typechecker.rs — Algorithm W inference
- src/effect_checker.rs — effect + capability analysis
- src/jit/ — Cranelift JIT with SIMD auto-vectorization
- src/ai/ — LLM client, memory, pipelines, debates, supervisors`;

  const button = document.getElementById('copy-markdown-btn');
  if (button) {

  button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(MARKDOWN);
      button.classList.add('copied');
      const originalHTML = button.innerHTML;
      button.innerHTML = '<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Copied!';
      setTimeout(() => {
        button.classList.remove('copied');
        button.innerHTML = originalHTML;
      }, 2000);
    } catch {
      // Clipboard API unavailable — no-op
    }
  });
  }
</script>
